{"name":"Blush Bomb","hex":"#dd99aa","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blush","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of blushing; a pink or red glow on the face caused by embarrassment, shame, shyness, love, etc.","A glow; a flush of colour, especially pink or red."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become red or pink in the face (and sometimes experience an associated feeling of warmth), especially due to shyness, love, shame, excitement, or embarrassment.","To be shy, ashamed, or embarrassed (to do something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blush"},{"term":"bomb","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An explosive device used or intended as a weapon, especially, one dropped from an aircraft.\n\n The atomic bomb.","The atomic bomb."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To attack using one or more bombs; to bombard.\n\n To attack or annoy in the manner of a bombing.","To attack or annoy in the manner of a bombing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bomb"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bomb","blocks":[{"text":"A bomb is an explosive weapon that uses the exothermic reaction of an explosive material to provide an extremely sudden and violent release of energy. Detonations inflict damage principally through ground- and atmosphere-transmitted mechanical stress, the impact and penetration of pressure-driven projectiles, pressure damage, and explosion-generated effects. Bombs have been utilized since the 11th century starting in East Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Saarlouis_Bombe.jpg/330px-Saarlouis_Bombe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bomb","wikidata":"Q127197"},{"title":"Blush (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Blush is a medium bright tone of pink."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Blush_rose_1.jpg/330px-Blush_rose_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_